-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where", "if", "unless" or "in the case of" not met).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a bare "must" not done, a permission outside its own wording).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Oaths and Declarations Act and Forms 82 and 83 are not among the sources: what they say is an input.
-- This Order fixes no period, so no time is counted in it (O 3 r 3 plays no part).

